      "title": "Almost two-thirds of Australians bulk-billed for all GP care amid extra incentives for doctors",
      "link": "https://www.theguardian.com/australia-news/2026/oct/26/almost-two-thirds-of-australians-bulk-billed-for-all-gp-care-amid-extra-incentives-for-doctors",
      "description": "<p>Exclusive: RACGP survey reflects Medicare investments, but experts caution quality of care and outcomes also matter</p><ul><li><p>Get our <a href=\"https://www.theguardian.com/email-newsletters?CMP=cvau_sfl\">new political email</a>, <a href=\"https://app.adjust.com/w4u7jx3\">free app</a> or <a href=\"https://www.theguardian.com/australia-news/series/full-story?CMP=cvau_sfl\">daily news podcast</a></p></li></ul><p>The proportion of general practitioners bulk-billing all of their patients has more than doubled in a year, a report has found, after the government introduced financial incentives for doctors and practices.</p><p>And almost two-thirds (63%) of Australians are now bulk-billed for all their GP care, up from 56% in both 2024 and 2025, which the report says is “likely a reflection of the federal government’s recent investment in Medicare bulk billing incentives”.</p> <a href=\"https://www.theguardian.com/australia-news/2026/oct/26/almost-two-thirds-of-australians-bulk-billed-for-all-gp-care-amid-extra-incentives-for-doctors\">Continue reading...</a>",
      "source_name": "The Guardian World",
      "published": "2026-10-25T14:00:06"
    },
    {
      "title": "‘Unusually large’ multi-state storm causing severe weather for Australia’s east – with more on the way",
      "link": "https://www.theguardian.com/australia-news/2026/oct/25/unusual-multi-state-storm-causing-flood-warningd-and-severe-weather-for-australias-east",
      "description": "<p>BoM predicts hail, damaging winds, flash flooding and power outages across southern Queensland, western NSW, the ACT and eastern Victoria on Sunday afternoon</p><ul><li><p>Get our <a href=\"https://www.theguardian.com/email-newsletters?CMP=cvau_sfl\">breaking news email</a>, <a href=\"https://app.adjust.com/w4u7jx3\">free app</a> or <a href=\"https://www.theguardian.com/australia-news/series/full-story?CMP=cvau_sfl\">daily news podcast</a></p></li></ul><p>Large parts of eastern Australia were put on alert for severe thunderstorms on Sunday afternoon with more potential storms and flood risk in store for Monday.</p><p>On Sunday afternoon, the Bureau of Meteorology issued a severe thunderstorm warning for Sydney, greater Wollongong and parts of Blue Mountains, Hawkesbury, Gosford, Wyong and Wollondilly, Wingecarribee areas.</p> <a href=\"https://www.theguardian.com/australia-news/2026/oct/25/unusual-multi-state-storm-causing-flood-warningd-and-severe-weather-for-australias-east\">Continue reading...</a>",
      "source_name": "The Guardian World",
      "published": "2026-10-25T05:30:30"
    },
    {
      "title": "AFP boss says politicians’ heated rhetoric is fuelling threats against MPs",
      "link": "https://www.theguardian.com/australia-news/2026/oct/25/afp-commissioner-krissy-barrett-threats-mps-political-debate-ntwnfb",
      "description": "<p>Commissioner Krissy Barrett says women are more often singled out, often with threats of sexual violence</p><ul><li><p>Get our <a href=\"https://www.theguardian.com/email-newsletters?CMP=cvau_sfl\">breaking news email</a>, <a href=\"https://app.adjust.com/w4u7jx3\">free app</a> or <a href=\"https://www.theguardian.com/australia-news/series/full-story?CMP=cvau_sfl\">daily news podcast</a></p></li></ul><p>Australia’s top federal law enforcement official has drawn a direct link between politicians’ rhetoric and threats and abuse being directed at leaders.</p><p>The safety of elected representatives at all levels has been thrown into the spotlight after independent MP Helen Haines was allegedly deliberate attacked outside her Wangaratta electoral office.</p> <a href=\"https://www.theguardian.com/australia-news/2026/oct/25/afp-commissioner-krissy-barrett-threats-mps-political-debate-ntwnfb\">Continue reading...</a>",
